  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Lantana trifolia",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lantana_trifolia",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1379378632,
      "text": "Lantana trifolia is a species of shrub in the family of Verbenaceae which is native to Central and South America but also has been introduced in parts of Sub-Saharan Africa and South/Southeast Asia. It bears beautiful flowers and small edible fruit. Its roots and leaves have been used in traditional ethnomedicines against a large variety of diseases."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Lantana trifolia",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lantana_trifolia",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 153112757,
      "text": "El cariaquito morado, Lantana trifolia, es un arbusto perenne con 3 hojas en cada nudo; las hojas lanceoladas, con glándulas anaranjadas en la cara inferior, con espigas densas y cilíndricas, con las brácteas inferiores largamente puntiagudas; frutos maduros jugosos y de color lilas o púrpuras."
    }
  },
